  "body": "**Unit Name:** `DistributionCreator`\n\n**Location:** `DistributionCreator.sol` - function `_createCampaign` (uses `_computeFees` and `_pullTokens`)\n\n**Description:** \nThe minimum reward-per-epoch check uses the gross `newCampaign.amount` before fees: `(newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount` reverts only if the pre-fee rate is too low. Immediately after, fees are deducted and `newCampaign.amount` is overwritten with `campaignAmountMinusFees`, which is the actual distributed amount. This allows campaigns whose NET per-epoch amount falls below `rewardTokenMinAmounts[token]`, violating the intended invariant “minimum per-epoch reward for validity.” Attackers can pass the check by supplying a large gross amount and a high fee rebate configuration that reduces the net amount below the threshold. Validate against post-fee amounts (or recompute threshold after fees) to preserve campaign validity guarantees.\n\n**PoC Summary:** `test/poc/DistributionCreator_min_threshold_checked_on_gross_not_net.t.sol` — The test creates a 1-hour campaign whose gross amount passes `_createCampaign`’s per-epoch check but, after 50% fees, the net-per-epoch falls below `rewardTokenMinAmounts`, expecting a revert with `Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow`; since the contract validates the minimum on gross before fees, `createCampaign` does not revert, causing the test to fail and confirming the bug. Verdict: true positive.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { C4PoC } from \"./C4PoC.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { Errors } from \"../../contracts/utils/Errors.sol\";\n\ncontract C4POC_min_threshold_checked_on_gross_not_net is C4PoC {\n    function test_min_threshold_checked_on_gross_not_net() public {\n        // 1. Set fee to 50% (5e8 / 1e9)\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFees(5e8);\n\n        // C4PoC sets min amount for angle to 1e8 (100 units)\n        uint256 minAmount = 1e8;\n\n        // 2. Create campaign where Gross > Min but Net < Min\n        // Gross = 1.2e8. Fee = 50% = 0.6e8. Net = 0.6e8.\n        // Net < Min (0.6e8 < 1e8), so it should fail if checked correctly.\n        // Gross > Min (1.2e8 > 1e8), so it passes currently.\n        \n        uint256 grossAmount = 120000000; // 1.2e8\n        \n        CampaignParameters memory p;\n        p.creator = alice;\n        p.rewardToken = address(angle);\n        p.amount = grossAmount;\n        p.campaignType = 0;\n        p.startTimestamp = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        p.duration = EPOCH_DURATION; // 1 hour\n        p.campaignData = hex\"\";\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        // This call succeeds due to the bug (checks gross amount).\n        // If fixed, it would revert with CampaignRewardTooLow.\n        creator.createCampaign(p);\n        \n        // If we reached here, bug confirmed.\n    }\n}\n```",
